# bat — Minimal base16 (see COLOURS.md).
#
# The themes themselves live in ~/.config/bat/themes/. bat only sees them once
# its cache has been rebuilt:
#
#     bat cache --build
#
# `just install` does this for you. `bat --list-themes` should then show
# minimal-dark and minimal-light.

# Both variants are declared, and --theme pins which one is used, the same way
# helix and zellij pin theirs. Swap to "light" here for the light palette, or to
# "auto" to let bat query the terminal's background colour and pick per-run.
--theme-dark="minimal-dark"
--theme-light="minimal-light"
--theme="dark"

# The themes italicise comments, matching cozy/helix/themes/minimal-*.toml. bat
# suppresses italics unless asked, so ask.
--italic-text=always
